In article <1993Apr15.152222.24453@mfltd.co.uk> dnh@mfltd.co.uk writes:
>> Suppose it were a +3 trident...
>Okay, but I thought humans counted as medium sized creatures?  In which
>case it would be d6+1+3 = 10 max?  I guess it's the only explanation tho' - unless it was a bloody strong hobbit :-)

No, the explanation is that damage for weapons is calculated differently for
monsters with weapons.  If a monster has an attack which does 1-6 damage (like
a hobbit does), and uses a weapon, it does 1-6 points of damage _plus_ weapon
damage.  (Players, including polymorphed players, don't get this benefit.)
